Tark page translation on the Mac: the desktop surfaces (ported from
Android's page-translate-ui.patch; Mac only, see windows/ and linux/
mac-only-patches.txt and android/desktop-only-patches.txt).

Translate is offered (the omnibox icon and bubble, "Translate to …" in the
page's menu, Translate in the app menu) only where Tark's own translator
can translate the page: Settings › Languages › Page translation on, a
language pair the Mac has a model for (TarkPageTranslation::CanOffer; no
Spanish on the Mac), and in a Private window only with the models already
here. --translate-script-url is ignored; Partial Translate (Google's) is
off. TranslateClient gains TarkCanOffer and TarkReadyToTranslate; the
first Translate of a pair downloads its models from gettarka.com (never
for an automatic translation) and the bubble shows "Getting translation
ready · N MB" (the manifest's size) until they are here. Translated, the
bubble's line is "Hindi → English · Show original". No Google branding:
the plain translate icon, no wordmark, no always-translate rules. The
Languages page gets the Page translation switch where Google's Translate
card was (removals/translate.patch). Supported languages: the 22 of India
and English. Browser tests: tark_page_translate_browsertest.cc; they give
captions' model store a temporary folder (--tark-captions-models-dir-for-
testing, honoured only in tests), never the person's own.

